s**.\n\n\n**Extracting Concise Data**\n\nI'm now streamlining the data extraction, with a strong emphasis on precision. My process targets the relevant information, such as \"Vitamin Deficiency Disease\" from page 6, and \"Urinary Incontinence\" from page 7, and eliminating all extraneous text. I am rigorously verifying the final output to ensure data integrity and accuracy and I've also verified that the extraneous text is correctly removed from the final page.\n\n\n**Parsing Relevant Sections**\n\nI am now extracting relevant segments focusing on the sections and removing extraneous introductory content such as title information I am concentrating on the core medical content from the input\n\n\n**Analyzing Key Definitions**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the extraction process to include definitions and key information. My goal is to extract the definitions from various entries, such as that for COPD and tuberculosis, and associate these with their respective disease names. I'm prioritizing the \"definition\" section and associating this with the corresponding heading. This should allow for a more streamlined presentation.\n\n\n**Defining Pulmonary Disorders**\n\nI'm now extracting definitions and key features for specific pulmonary disorders. I'm focusing on \"Bronchiectasis\" and \"Emphysema.\" I am successfully capturing their respective definitions and identifying their associated \"Common Clinical Features\" and \"Major Pathological Changes.\" My goal is to extract the core diagnostic criteria.\n\n\n**Defining Pleural Conditions**\n\nI'm now extracting definitions and key information regarding pleural conditions. I am focusing on \"Pleural Effusion\" and \"Pneumothorax,\" ensuring I accurately capture their definitions and classifications such as \"Major Types\" and \"Common Causes.\" My aim is to organize these details for clearer understanding.\n\n\n**Defining Respiratory Issues**\n\nI am now extracting definitions and classifications of respiratory condi